offer a range of support and services. Explore all UNCW has to offer!\nExplore Seahawk Life\nHousing\nLiving Off-Campus\nDining\nResearch\nResearch & Innovation\nStudent Research\nResearch Centers & Institutes\nMajor Research Programs\nInnovation & Commercialization\nSupport for Researchers\nLibrary\nKnowledge, Innovation, Discovery\nTeaching & Research Are Entwined at UNCW\nDelve deep into your interests through applied learning, where undergraduate and graduate students partner with faculty on high-quality research projects.\nLearn More\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nSTEM Designated Programs\nHome\nSeahawk Life\nSupport & Success\nInternational\nInternational Students & Scholars\nSTEM Designated Programs\nOffice of International Students & Scholars\nOffice of International Students & Scholars\nProspective Students\nAbout Us\nResources\nPrograms & Events\nAdmitted\nSTEM Designated Programs\nImportant Changes to F & J Immigration Status\nUNCW offers undergraduate and graduate programs with CIP codes that make F-1 visa holders on Optional Practical Training eligible to apply for a two-year STEM OPT extension.\nInternational students with an F-1 visa who earned a UNCW bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s or doctoral degree in a STEM Designated Program, as defined by the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS), have the option to apply for a 24-month OPT extension after their first year of standard OPT. This means they may be eligible to obtain a total of 36 months of OPT work experience in the U.S.\nFor more information about the program and processes for international students studying in the U.S., please visit the DHS website.\nUNCW offers the following:\nPrograms\nUndergraduate\nProgram Name\nCIP Code\nCIP Description\nBiology, B.A.\n26.0101\nBiology/Biological Sciences, General\nBiology, B.S.\n26.0101\nBiology/Biological Sciences, General\nChemistry, B.A.\n40.0501\nChemistry, General\nChemistry, B.S.\n40.0501\nChemistry, General\nCoastal Engineering, B.S.\n14.9999\nEngineering, Other\nComputer Science, B.S.\n11.0701\nComputer Science\nCybersecurity, B.S.\n11.1003\nComputer and Information Systems Security/Auditing/Information Assurance\nDigital Arts, B.A.\n11.0803\nComputer Graphics\nEnvironmental Sciences, B.S.\n3.0104\nEnvironmental Science\nGeology, B.S.\n40.0601\nGeology/Earth Science, General\nGeosciences, B.A.\n40.0601\nGeology/Earth Science, General\nInformation Technology, B.S.\n11.0103\nInformation Technology\nIntelligent Systems Engineering, B.S.\n14.9999\nEngineering, Other\nMarine Biology, B.S.\n26.1302\nMarine Biology and Biological Oceanography\nMathematics, B.A.\n27.0101\nMathematics, General\nMathematics, B.S.\n27.0101\nMathematics, General\nOceanography, B.S.\n40.0607\nOceanography, Chemical and Physical\nPhysics, B.A.\n40.0801\nPhysics, General\nPhysics, B.S.\n40.0801\nPhysics, General\nStatistics, B.S.\n27.0501\nStatistics, General\nGraduate\nProgram Name\nCIP Code\nCIP Description\nAccountancy, MSAC\n30.7104\nFinancial Analytics\nApplied Coastal & Ocean Sciences, Ph.D.\n30.3201\nMarine Sciences\nBiology, M.S.\n26.0101\nBiology/Biological Sciences, General\nBusiness Administration (International), MBA\n52.1301\nManagement Science\nBusiness Analytics, M.S.\n52.1399\nManagement Sciences and Quantitative Methods, Other\nChemistry, M.S.\n40.0501\nChemistry, General\nCoastal & Ocean Policy, M.S.\n3.0205\nWater, Wetlands, and Marine Resources Management\nComputer Science & Information Systems, M.S.\n11.0101\nComputer and Information Sciences, General\nData Science & Artificial Intelligence, M.S.\n11.0802\nData Modeling/Warehousing and Database Administration\nEnvironmental Sciences, M.S.\n3.0103\nEnvironmental Studies\nFinance & Investment Management, M.S.\n30.7104\nFinancial Analytics\nGeoscience, M.S.\n40.0601\nGeology/Earth Science, General\nIntegrative, Comparative & Marine Biology, Ph.D.\n26.9999\nBiological and Biomedical Sciences, Other\nMarine Biology, M.S.\n26.1302\nMarine Biology and Biological Oceanography\nMarine